<title>FRANCE: SWISSAIR, SABENA ORDER AIRBUS A330-200 PLANES.</title>
<headline>SWISSAIR, SABENA ORDER AIRBUS A330-200 PLANES.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>European plane making consortium Airbus Industrie said on Wedesday Swissair had ordered nine A330-200 long-range twin aircraft while Belgium's Sabena signed for four planes.</p>
<p>Swissair owns 49.5 percent in Sabena.</p>
<p>Airbus Industrie  is made up of French state-owned Ste Nationale Industrielle Aerospatiale, British Aerospace Plc , Daimler-Benz Aerospace, a unit of Daimler-Benz AG and Construcciones Aeronauticas SA (CASA) of Spain.</p>
</text>
